4,-0.027648847550153732,0.0021775488276034594,0.0860840454697609,-0.05355481430888176,0.07524968683719635,0.08893463760614395],"metadata":{"id":"15b5da4a-c281-41ff-8f2d-ece05e80d604","url":"file:///app/collector/hotdir/OpenCore Legacy Patcher Process for Unsupported Macs.md","title":"OpenCore Legacy Patcher Process for Unsupported Macs.md","docAuthor":"Unknown","description":"Unknown","docSource":"a text file uploaded by the user.","chunkSource":"","published":"7/4/2025, 6:37:19 AM","wordCount":239,"token_count_estimate":386,"text":"<document_metadata>\nsourceDocument: OpenCore Legacy Patcher Process for Unsupported Macs.md\npublished: 7/4/2025, 6:37:19 AM\n</document_metadata>\n\n# OpenCore Legacy Patcher (OCLP) for Unsupported Mac Installation\n\n## Key Learning: Use OCLP Instead of Manual OpenCore for Legacy Macs\n\n### Problem Solved\n- **Issue**: 2012 MacBook Pro (MacBookPro9,2) wouldn't recognize manually created OpenCore USB installers as bootable\n- **Root Cause**: Manual OpenCore configuration missing legacy-specific patches and drivers\n- **Solution**: OpenCore Legacy Patcher (OCLP) automates the entire process\n\n### OCLP Workflow\n1. **Create Installer** (on any Mac):\n   - Launch OCLP app\n   - Select \"Create macOS Installer\"\n   - Choose target macOS version (e.g., Ventura)\n   - Select USB drive\n   - OCLP downloads and patches automatically\n\n2. **Universal Installer**: \n   - Installer works on ANY supported Mac\n   - No need to specify target Mac during creation\n   - Hardware detection happens at boot time"}},{"id":"9e0f49cb-6d53-42e7-9425-4f43358f9dd8","values":[-0.029452605172991753,-0.00802268274128437,0.049909427762031555,-0.02137409895658493,0.12554974853992462,-0.08482562005519867,-0.06320911645889282,0.06048222631216049,-0.07893705368041992,-0.018445271998643875,0.08575630187988281,-0.01842900738120079,-0.05275189131498337,0.019596677273511887,0.008475254289805889,0.10455221682786942,0.05036056414246559,0.0007692129584029317,0.0534164160